mm/page_reporting: the cycle delay is a runtime parameter

A reporting request waits two seconds for more pages to accumulate before a
cycle runs, and a cycle's budget is a fraction of each free list. Right for
a guest churning memory, where every reported page it reuses is a fault on
the host (measured: eight times upstream's rate made a pnpm install take
four times as long). Wrong for a guest that has just trimmed its cache and
is idle: with 2 MiB blocks freed by a trim the budget comes to one report a
cycle, and the Mac saw the guest's footprint fall by a hundred megabytes
every two seconds for twenty seconds. page_reporting_delay_ms, writable, is
what lets the guest's agent ask for the freed memory back now and restore
the two seconds once it has gone.

--- a/mm/page_reporting.c
+++ b/mm/page_reporting.c
@@ -47,7 +47,16 @@ MODULE_PARM_DESC(page_reporting_order, "Set page reporting order");
  */
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(page_reporting_order);
 
-#define PAGE_REPORTING_DELAY	(2 * HZ)
+/* How long a reporting request waits for more pages to accumulate before a
+ * cycle runs. Two seconds is right for a guest that is churning memory —
+ * every reported page it reuses is a fault on the host — and wrong for one
+ * that has just trimmed its cache and is idle: a runtime knob lets its agent
+ * ask for the freed memory to go back now.
+ */
+static unsigned int page_reporting_delay_ms = 2000;
+module_param(page_reporting_delay_ms, uint, 0644);
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(page_reporting_delay_ms, "Delay before a reporting cycle, in milliseconds");
+#define PAGE_REPORTING_DELAY	msecs_to_jiffies(page_reporting_delay_ms)
 static struct page_reporting_dev_info __rcu *pr_dev_info __read_mostly;
 
 enum {
